      "takeaway": "RouteRLT targets the problem that pretrained VLA models lose precision during contact-rich phases such as connector insertion and cable management, where refining the whole policy with RL risks eroding generalist behavior. The framework learns a phase selector deciding when and which phase-specific RL specialist takes control, plus a stabilizer for transient switches and an action-boundary manager for transitions between chunked policy outputs. In LIBERO multi-object pick-and-place, the learned routing improves over the base VLA and matches routing with privileged phase boundaries without accessing them at deployment; a real cable pickup and port-insertion task validates automatic handoff to pickup and insertion specialists. Inspect how the selector is trained and how boundary handling preserves chunked action continuity.",
